# The workspace legitimately spans two React majors: the panel micro-frontends
# (apps/panel/*, apps/product/**) are React 18, while apps/web, apps/web_old and
# apps/docs are React 19. Runtime resolution handles that fine — pnpm gives each
# package the peer variant it asked for.
#
# TypeScript does NOT. pnpm hoists every transitive package into the virtual
# store's shared node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules, and when two versions of a
# package exist there only one wins. @types/react@19 won, so tsc — which walks
# UP from .pnpm/<pkg>/node_modules when resolving a dependency's types — handed
# React 19's ReactNode to the React 18 apps. Every JSX element in every React 18
# app then failed with TS2786 ("cannot be used as a JSX component", bigint is
# not assignable to ReactNode), which made `turbo run check-types` useless as a
# gate. Excluding the React typings from hoisting keeps each app on the
# @types/react its own package.json asks for.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
